posts.body:
@ShadowDragon
I believe Zia_ is right and that it's more about reimagining UI beyond those basics of what is typically seen with RPG Maker. And, I mean, I don't think regular game jams are worth it personally--why put in work to make what's usually a very short game? I personally only care about making long games with a lot of character interaction, so I never participate in game jams. You don't have to participate in the UI competition if you're not interested lol.
Besides, I'd say the theme would just be for guidance, but it's not as if the bones of a custom UI can't be reused for different projects. Think about many plugins: they're templates, generalized to have the best use for the most people, but often customizable and meant to not just be plug-and-play, but instead for you to mess with parameters and note tags in order to form the plugin to your own game. If this UI thing were to actually happen, I know I'd release the demo with mine for anyone to edit and use if they want to (and maybe others would too, idk). But even if someone didn't want to take the whole UI and use it, someone might get inspired by just seeing something unique done in RPG Maker the way Zia_ is YeXin's work (me too, omg it looks so good
@YeXin
).
Anyway, I highly recommend checking out this video to see that UI design is so much more than some custom pictures~
